{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_e02151f8817d64435c43b0470cb7499c4702069cef270a2e7fc2b147eb16f2b5", "title": "Around the World (Red Hot Chili Peppers song)", "text": "\"Around the World\" is a song by Red Hot Chili Peppers released as the second single from their 1999 album, \"Californication\". The single peaked at number seven on the \"Billboard\" Modern Rock Tracks and number sixteen on the Mainstream Rock Tracks.", "score": 48.0246}, {"id": "hp_doc_3ad3c97f084ef7f200917c3910768cf84957731ef662d680cc99ab1a4a048abc", "title": "Ataxia (band)", "text": "Ataxia was a short-lived American experimental rock band formed in 2004 by guitarist John Frusciante (Red Hot Chili Peppers), bassist Joe Lally (Fugazi) and drummer Josh Klinghoffer (Red Hot Chili Peppers, Dot Hacker, The Bicycle Thief), who later succeeded Frusciante as the lead guitarist of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.", "score": 41.2182}, {"id": "hp_doc_e074b9d67592f76ce001db13ad88857ecd6f16b172a1d75fa71127d3d0854c90", "title": "Silverlake Conservatory of Music", "text": "Silverlake Conservatory of Music is a nonprofit educational organization formed in California. It was founded in 2001 by Red Hot Chili Peppers bassist, Michael \"Flea\" Balzary and Keith \"Tree\" Barry (longtime touring musician with the Chili Peppers) to foster music education, with Chili Pepper's member Anthony Kiedis also on the board. The facility organizes an annual \"Hullabaloo\", one of which featured performances by Red Hot Chili Peppers, Eddie Vedder and Charlie Haden, and the Chili Peppers raised $1 million for the Conservatory during an August 24, 2011 performance at Club Nokia.", "score": 37.4775}], "remaining_searches": 2}
