{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_f16749185c2740af9987d44c19b7550aef0018b4a9596a4deb7eaf73d831471d", "title": "Californication (album)", "text": "Californication is the seventh studio album by American rock band Red Hot Chili Peppers. It was released on June 8, 1999, on Warner Bros. Records and was produced by Rick Rubin. \"Californication\" marked the return of John Frusciante, who had previously appeared on \"Mother's Milk\" and \"Blood Sugar Sex Magik\", to replace Dave Navarro as the band's guitarist. Frusciante's return was credited with changing the band's sound altogether, producing a notable shift in style from the music recorded with Navarro. The album's subject material incorporated various sexual innuendos commonly associated with the band, but also contained more varied themes than previous outings, including lust, death, contemplations of suicide, California, drugs, globalization, and travel.", "score": 14.0406}, {"id": "hp_doc_e02151f8817d64435c43b0470cb7499c4702069cef270a2e7fc2b147eb16f2b5", "title": "Around the World (Red Hot Chili Peppers song)", "text": "\"Around the World\" is a song by Red Hot Chili Peppers released as the second single from their 1999 album, \"Californication\". The single peaked at number seven on the \"Billboard\" Modern Rock Tracks and number sixteen on the Mainstream Rock Tracks.", "score": 11.7704}, {"id": "hp_doc_debe4300d7e1ac4e1e56da88f5f78ea251ddbb180fbdce1f9d8dd8fd448d2fd0", "title": "John Frusciante discography", "text": "The discography of John Frusciante, who is best known as the former guitarist of the rock band Red Hot Chili Peppers, consists of eleven solo albums and four EPs, as well as two albums with collaborators Joe Lally and Josh Klinghoffer under the name Ataxia and one EP and one album under the alias of Trickfinger. Frusciante left the Red Hot Chili Peppers in 1992 after he got tired of the growing success of the band. He released his first solo album, \"Niandra LaDes and Usually Just a T-Shirt\", in 1994 on American Recordings. His second record, \"Smile From the Streets You Hold\", was released in 1997 and later taken off the market at his request in 1999. After returning to the Red Hot Chili Peppers in 1998, Frusciante recorded \"Californication\" with the band and subsequently released his third solo album, \"To Record Only Water for Ten Days\", in February 2001 on Warner Music Group.", "score": 8.4971}], "remaining_searches": 1}
